@startuml
' ==========================================================================
' docs/project/Core_Architecture.puml   (REPLACEMENT)
'
' The version in the repository is stale and now contradicts the thesis. It
' describes a four-stage "RL-Verification" pipeline with a reward function
' feeding an RL loop, a "P4 Tool", and no repair, judge, or mutation scoring.
' Two problems with leaving it in place:
'
'   1. The thesis explicitly corrects the RL framing. The loop is iterative
'      prompting with quantitative feedback over an external API; no model is
'      trained. A committee member who browses the repository would find a
'      diagram asserting the framing Chapter 4 disowns.
'   2. It omits the repair stage, the judge, and the mutation-based confidence,
'      which are two of the three claimed contributions.
'
' This replacement is self-contained (no !include) so it renders anywhere in
' the docs tree. It is the same structure as the thesis figure, so the two
' cannot drift apart silently.
' ==========================================================================
title qallm-uva: core architecture

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle uml2
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF9
  BorderColor #5C6BC0
  FontColor #1A237E
}
skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #90A4AE
  FontStyle italic
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F

package "Presentation" {
  [CLI]           as CLI
  [Notebook]      as MAGIC
  [Web UI]        as WEB
  [REST API]      as API
}

package "Orchestration" {
  [Orchestrator]  as ORCH
  [Jobs]          as JOBS
  [Profiles]      as PROF
  [Budget guard]  as COST
}

package "Assessment pipeline" {
  [Ingestion]     as ING
  [Analysis]      as ANA
  [Verification]  as VER
  [Repair]        as REP
  [Judge]         as JUD
}

package "Reporting" {
  [Reporter]      as RPT
  [Metrics]       as MET
  [Provenance]    as PRV
}

interface "StaticCodeAnalyzer" as IANA
interface "LLMModel"           as ILLM
interface "Judge"              as IJUD

CLI   --> ORCH
MAGIC --> ORCH
WEB   --> API
API   --> JOBS
JOBS  --> ORCH
PROF  ..> ORCH
COST  ..> ORCH

ORCH --> ING
ING  --> ANA : units
ANA  --> VER : findings
VER  --> REP : defects
REP  --> JUD : variant
JUD  --> ORCH : verdict

ANA -left-( IANA
VER -left-( ILLM
REP -right-( ILLM
JUD -left-( IJUD

VER --> RPT
JUD --> RPT
RPT --> MET
RPT --> PRV

note bottom
  The verification loop is iterative prompting with quantitative
  feedback over an external LLM API. No model is trained.
end note
@enduml
